'''TANAKA HIROSHI TESTIFIES: "I SIGNED THE LICENSES" — Former Deputy Director General Admits Approving Waste Export Licenses Without Inspection; "I Was Told the Inspections Were Completed. They Were Not." — PPO Investigation Accelerates'''
Former Deputy Director General Tanaka Hiroshi testified before the PPO special prosecutor today. Tanaka — who oversaw the Ministry of Environment's waste export licensing division from 2021 to 2025 — admitted to signing 14 waste export licenses without verifying that pre-export inspections had been conducted. Tanaka's testimony: "I signed the licenses. I was told the inspections were completed. They were not. I did not verify. I should have verified. The system relied on trust. The trust was broken." The licenses permitted the export of 40,000 tonnes of processed waste to Balisca — the waste now blockaded at the Port of Castejón. The Okami Times notes: Tanaka signed 14 licenses without inspection. 40,000 tonnes of waste sits in Castejón. The system relied on trust. The trust was broken. The question is: who told Tanaka the inspections were completed? Who broke the trust? And how many more Tanakas are there in the Ministry of Environment?

'''AKAMATSU GROUP: COURT APPEARANCE — Three Defendants Appear; Bail Denied; Akamatsu Seijiro Silent; Ibuki Yuma Weeps; Izumida Shotaro: "I Was Following Orders"; "The Hierarchy Is Clear"'''
The three Akamatsu Group leaders appeared in Okami District Court today. Akamatsu Seijiro, 45, chairman — silent throughout the 20-minute hearing. Ibuki Yuma, 31, executive VP and former entertainer — wept openly. Izumida Shotaro, 48, CFO advisor — told the court: "I was following orders. The instructions came from the chairman's office." The prosecutor requested continued detention. The judge denied bail for all three. Next hearing: July 17. The Okami Times notes: Ibuki Yuma wept. Izumida Shotaro blamed the chairman. Akamatsu Seijiro said nothing. The hierarchy is clear. The chairman gave the orders. The executive VP deflected the scrutiny. The CFO advisor moved the money. The workers paid. The executives stole. "I was following orders" is not a defence. It is a confession that the hierarchy existed. It is a confession that the system was designed to exploit the workers and protect the executives.

'''FM PRESS CONFERENCE: AFTERMATH — PPO Plans Oversight Hearing; Ayorin Community Meeting Friday; "The FM Spoke. The Questions Remain."; "The Apology Is a Beginning. It Is Not an Ending."'''
The FM's press conference continues to reverberate. PPO Diet Affairs Chair Sadanuma: "The PPO will request an oversight hearing with the Foreign Minister in the Diet next week. The FM must explain the delay. 'A failure of communication' is not an explanation." Ayorin community meeting Friday in Suminoe ward. Community chair Burawa Yuki: "The apology is a beginning. It is not an ending. The community will meet Friday. The community will decide what comes next." The Okami Times notes: the FM spoke. The questions remain. The Diet will ask. The community will meet. The FM's words will be tested. "A failure of communication, not a failure of action" — but the failure of communication IS the failure of action. The FM must explain. The FM must answer. The apology is accepted. The delay is not explained.

